g_trends'. The registry's evaluate() dispatches each spec atomically to ONE MetricValue OR ONE Unavailable (no per-dimension unavailability), so AC-3's 'detected_by degrades to unavailable without affecting others' is only natively achievable if each dimension is its own spec — yet AC-1's 'a bug_trends lens with the five dimensions' plus the in-payload MISSING-bucket mechanism read as a single spec. The two mechanisms cannot both hold under one spec.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff9a67fd257872681","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach + Acceptance Criteria (AC-1, AC-3); Testing ('detected_by absent everywhere -> dimension reports unavailable, other dimensions unaffected')","norm_id":"ncf7cfdd9bf51e3b8","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["detected_by empty everywhere but close_class/age/etc. have data: a single bug_trends spec computes a non-None payload, so evaluate() yields a MetricValue — AC-3's 'that dimension reports unavailable' has no registry expression and the plan defines no in-payload unavailable convention, risking conflation of 'dimension unavailable' with an empty distribution (the empty-implies-healthy failure the Testing section explicitly forbids)"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State that register() appends five sibling specs (e.g. bug_close_class_distribution, bug_detected_by_distribution, bug_open_age, bug_caused_by_fanin, bug_time_to_close), each lens='bug_trends', source='structural', confidence='high'; the detected_by spec's compute returns None when the field is absent everywhere, yielding Unavailable for that spec only.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alter